# gensym-with-scope produces unique symbols with explicit scope character.
# Prelude wrapper: [gensym-with-scope scope prefix] → calls [builtin-gensym scope prefix]
# Format: "{scope}ꜱʏᴍ⧼{prefix}⧽{N}" where N is a global monotonic counter.
# Two calls with the same scope+prefix must produce distinct strings (counter advances).
# Counter values are NOT pinned: the global AtomicU64 is shared across all tests in
# the binary. The test outputs only the uniqueness result, not the raw gensym strings.
[a: [gensym-with-scope "ℊ" "test"]]
[b: [gensym-with-scope "ℊ" "test"]]
[not [= a b]]
=== out
Variant(Boolean.True, Null)
